# --- Rust ---
# Build artifacts (cargo default output dir).
/target

# Cargo.lock IS committed. The usual "libraries don't commit lockfiles"
# convention optimizes for downstream resolution flexibility — which is
# preserved, because consumers ignore a dependency's committed lock. What we
# gain is REPRODUCIBLE CI: the MSRV job resolves the SAME dependency graph on
# every run, so a transitive update can't silently move the real MSRV floor,
# and the `tests/guard.rs` closure assertions can't go red for a reason that
# has nothing to do with this crate. (So: NO `Cargo.lock` entry here.)

# --- Lean (formal/) ---
.lake/
formal/.lake/

# --- Python (packaging lands in C3) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# --- editors / OS ---
*.swp
.DS_Store
